seg-bf0c90f5c02a = The notification is <c1/>, <c2/>, <c3/> or <c4/>. It is cleared by publishing state <c5/>, not <c6/>: a consumer that only treats <c7/> as cleared should treat <c8/> as cleared too. By default the <b>degraded</b> band gives <c9/> and the <b>untrusted</b> band gives <c10/>, with <c11/>. It is lowered after <c12/> epochs at a better state. If no epoch arrives for <c13/> seconds it warns that the score is not being updated. Calibration never raises a notification. The <c14/> source carries no <c15/> list (the sentence has the band, score and the top two reasons only).

