seg-4226afc6175c = In OpenCPN: Options, Connections, Add Connection, <b>Network</b>, protocol <b>TCP</b>, address <c1/>, port <c2/>, direction <b>Input</b>. While trust is not collapsed the stream is the receiver's own, plus a <c3/> sentence per cycle. While it is collapsed the forwarded GGA has quality <c4/>, RMC status <c5/>, and the mode indicators say no fix, with checksums recomputed: the equipment sees the receiver itself declare the fix invalid and raises its own alarm. The <c6/> sentences are visible in OpenCPN's NMEA debug window (Options, Connections, "NMEA debug window"). The position fields are left as received.

