seg-7a5ac2d2f229 = <c1/> is a score panel for OpenCPN (score, band, gate, top reasons, an alert when trust becomes untrusted) that reads <c2/> from OpenCPN's own NMEA stream, so it needs no connection beyond the one above. It is built with CMake against the OpenCPN plugin API header (vendored, with its source commit) and wxWidgets; <c3/> runs the wx-free logic tests and checks that the library exports the entry points OpenCPN looks up. It has been run inside OpenCPN { "5.8.4" } under a virtual display on the synthetic gated stream (OpenCPN handed <c4/> to the plugin, the panel went red, and OpenCPN's own position froze when the gate engaged; screenshots, log and script in <c5/>), but not on a real desktop, other versions or platforms, and it is not packaged for OpenCPN's plugin manager. See the plugin's <a1><c6/></a1>. It is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later, unlike the rest of the repository (<a2><c7/></a2>).

